1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,250
So, I was having a memory,

2
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:09,958
of the first story I wrote about my emotions.

3
00:00:09,958 --> 00:00:15,147
And the more I read, the more I was back inside my mind.

4
00:00:18,276 --> 00:00:21,446
And my fear kept pulling the fire alarm.

5
00:00:22,083 --> 00:00:26,327
So I imagined myself as the CEO of my mind,

6
00:00:26,327 --> 00:00:28,731
looking around to see why.

7
00:00:28,731 --> 00:00:29,731
Fear?

8
00:00:30,221 --> 00:00:31,821
What are you looking at?

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,139
The Void.

10
00:00:39,375 --> 00:00:40,553
Huge.

11
00:00:41,463 --> 00:00:42,763
Unmoving.

12
00:00:43,683 --> 00:00:46,443
And its face was pure darkness.

13
00:00:47,207 --> 00:00:48,767
It's going to hurt me.

14
00:00:49,302 --> 00:00:50,812
It hasn't moved.

15
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:52,847
That's what scares me.

16
00:00:53,327 --> 00:00:54,917
It's not safe here.

17
00:00:55,375 --> 00:00:57,308
Nothing is going to hurt you.

18
00:00:57,750 --> 00:00:58,958
You don't know that.

19
00:01:02,196 --> 00:01:04,792
Out! Everybody out!

20
00:01:04,792 --> 00:01:06,125
We always come back.

21
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:10,810
Panic attacks, forcing every emotion out of my mind.

22
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:12,450
Causing chaos.

23
00:01:13,684 --> 00:01:15,094
Then one day,

24
00:01:15,094 --> 00:01:18,000
I put my hand on my fear's shoulder.

25
00:01:19,990 --> 00:01:22,830
You need to stop pulling the fire alarm.

26
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:25,119
It's causing turmoil.

27
00:01:25,751 --> 00:01:27,901
I'm only trying to keep us safe.

28
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:31,238
I can't.

29
00:01:31,698 --> 00:01:32,875
I'm sorry.

30
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:36,472
My fear refused.

31
00:01:38,583 --> 00:01:39,583
Fear,

32
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,083
we need to put you in a time-out.

33
00:01:45,502 --> 00:01:47,440
So I put my fear into a cage.

34
00:01:49,042 --> 00:01:51,148
Please don't leave me with it.

35
00:01:55,328 --> 00:02:00,042
I told myself it was the responsible thing to do.

36
00:02:00,042 --> 00:02:01,830
And I felt sadness.

37
00:02:04,452 --> 00:02:07,532
And the Void stood there, stone-faced,

38
00:02:07,532 --> 00:02:10,192
its shadow filling half the room.

39
00:02:13,564 --> 00:02:18,564
And then, when I wasn't looking, I had an image in my mind.

40
00:02:27,643 --> 00:02:29,303
Why are you doing this?

41
00:02:29,917 --> 00:02:31,708
You're going to hurt me.

42
00:02:31,708 --> 00:02:33,500
This is a trick.

43
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,154
This can't be right.

44
00:02:38,125 --> 00:02:40,201
This doesn't make any sense.

45
00:02:40,718 --> 00:02:42,518
You're supposed to hurt me.

46
00:02:42,876 --> 00:02:45,009
Why are you just standing there?

47
00:02:45,403 --> 00:02:47,936
Are you just here to scare me forever?

48
00:02:50,439 --> 00:02:52,729
And the Void did not move.

49
00:02:53,629 --> 00:02:55,149
It stood there.

50
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:02,517
This is it.

51
00:03:02,917 --> 00:03:06,734
My fear thought the Void had had enough of its complaining,

52
00:03:06,734 --> 00:03:08,394
and would destroy it.

53
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:13,046
But then, my fear felt a hand on its shoulder.

54
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:19,050
And it looked up, into the face of the Void.

55
00:03:23,338 --> 00:03:28,084
And instead of darkness, my fear saw the twinkling of lights.

56
00:03:28,084 --> 00:03:32,193
Like galaxies, and nebulae, and stars of the universe.

57
00:03:32,193 --> 00:03:35,460
The Void, filled with bits and pieces of meaning.

58
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:43,028
And for once, my fear wasn't afraid.

59
00:03:43,928 --> 00:03:46,758
It felt wonder, and amazement.

60
00:03:49,585 --> 00:03:51,555
Why are you showing me this?

61
00:03:56,064 --> 00:03:59,934
And the Void stared into the screen of my consciousness.

62
00:04:00,598 --> 00:04:03,258
My other emotions were looking back.

63
00:04:07,289 --> 00:04:11,979
They smiled, just for a moment, then went back to helping me.

64
00:04:14,667 --> 00:04:18,125
Then my fear felt the gentle push of the Void.

65
00:04:18,125 --> 00:04:19,958
The Void stood there,

66
00:04:19,958 --> 00:04:23,639
with galaxies twinkling in its dark facade.

67
00:04:32,333 --> 00:04:33,333
Fear.

68
00:04:33,792 --> 00:04:34,941
Can I help?

69
00:04:42,276 --> 00:04:46,669
The old cage had rusted, its gate hanging open.

70
00:04:46,669 --> 00:04:49,259
But that was just a small detail.

71
00:04:50,387 --> 00:04:54,500
Because the scene changed, to my emotions at the console.

72
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:57,185
And the Void, standing in the background.

73
00:04:57,185 --> 00:05:00,985
I could barely see that rusty cage anymore,

74
00:05:00,985 --> 00:05:02,905
in the back of my mind.

75
00:05:07,133 --> 00:05:08,443
After that,

76
00:05:09,072 --> 00:05:12,852
I may have shed a tear or two myself.

